directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n18:+| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n22:+### Starting a surfaced command\n23:+\n24:+The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n25:+\n26:+| Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n27:+|---|---|---|\n28:+| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\n29:+| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n30:+| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n31:+| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n32:+| Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n33:+| OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n34:+| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n35:+\n43:++-- dsh/\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n4:+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n9:-5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n10:+5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n18:+| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n22:+### Starting a surfaced command\n23:+\n24:+The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n25:+\n26:+| Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n27:+|---|---|---|\n28:+| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\n29:+| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n30:+| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n31:+| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n32:+| Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n33:+| OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n34:+| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n35:+\n43:++-- dsh/\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | rg -n \\\"parent-named|^\\\\+|^-\\\" | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532683092,"end":1794532683951}}}}
