{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532694396,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8507c1ffeeKHr8YUEWWSQ84","part":{"id":"prt_1d27bd0f7001hYGmu6trWd3wbV","sessionID":"ses_e2d8507c1ffeeKHr8YUEWWSQ84","messageID":"msg_1d27bc7400014FEnWBRiGvxapi","type":"text","text":"T026 done. I added one sentence to section 2, step 5 Render, in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n\nThe sentence reads: \"With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`.\"\n\nVerify, run from the repo root with `$HOOKDOC` = `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`:\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"parent-named only\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nExpected output was `1`, and it printed `1` with exit 0.\n\nTwo notes on the file. The diff for it also shows the DSH adapter row and the \"Starting a surfaced command\" subsection, which are other workers' T005 and T018 changes. I left them untouched. I did not tick the T026 checkbox, as instructed.\n\nNothing is blocked on the operator from my side.","time":{"start":1794532692215,"end":1794532694396}}}
